<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-5xl flex-col gap-6 px-6 py-12">
  <%= render FlatPack::Breadcrumb::Component.new(
    show_back: true,
    back_href: "javascript:window.history.back()",
    show_home: true,
    home_url: root_path,
    class: "mb-2"
  ) do |breadcrumb| %>
    <% breadcrumb.item(text: "Dummy app docs") %>
    <% breadcrumb.item(text: "Setup") %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Setup",
    subtitle: "What the host app needs before the addon can manage ordered item collections.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::Alert::Component.new(
    style: :info,
    title: "Prerequisite stack",
    description: "Install this addon into a Rails app that already has Recording Studio mounted and its recordable types registered."
  ) %>

  <div>
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Required before install",
      subtitle: "Baseline host app expectations.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <div>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6">
        <li>A Rails app with Recording Studio already mounted and working.</li>
        <li>Host parent and item recordable models registered the same way as the rest of your Recording Studio setup.</li>
        <li>A parent recordable that will opt into at least one named order group.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Install flow",
      subtitle: "Keep setup narrow and explicit.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <div>
      <div class="mt-4 bg-(--code-block-background-color) border border-(--code-block-border-color) rounded-lg">
        <div class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-(--code-block-border-color) text-sm font-medium text-(--code-block-title-color)">Code Example</div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap wrap-break-word"><code class="font-mono text-sm text-(--code-block-code-color)">bundle install
rails generate recording_studio_orderable:install
rails generate recording_studio_orderable:migrations
bin/rails db:migrate</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">If duplicate unnamed orders already exist, the migration keeps the newest default order and renames older duplicates so the new unique index can be added safely.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">Before exposing mounted named-list pages, configure <code>authorize_parent_recording</code> in the generated initializer. <code>authenticate_controller</code> and <code>current_owner_resolver</code> are optional overrides on top of actor-first defaults.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6">Opt parent recordables into one or more order groups after installation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Parent opt-in example",
      subtitle: "Use the DSL on the parent recordable that owns the ordered items.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <div>
      <div class="mt-4 bg-(--code-block-background-color) border border-(--code-block-border-color) rounded-lg">
        <div class="px-4 py-2 border-b border-(--code-block-border-color) text-sm font-medium text-(--code-block-title-color)">Code Example</div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap wrap-break-word"><code class="font-mono text-sm text-(--code-block-code-color)">class Folder &lt; ApplicationRecord
  include RecordingStudioOrderable::OrderableRecordable

  recording_studio_order_group :pages, allows: ["Page"]
end</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
      title: "Demo app verification",
      subtitle: "The included dummy app shows the expected host-owned docs flow, including drag-save notifications.",
      variant: :h3,
      class: "mb-0 pb-0"
    ) %>

    <div>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-6">
        <li>Launch the dummy app and sign in as the seeded admin user.</li>
        <li>Use the sidebar links to open the local docs pages and the mounted addon home page.</li>
        <li>Use the folder demo to confirm owner-scoped named lists and drag-to-reorder work after installation.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Notification integration:</strong> The drag-save UI supports two notification modes:
          <ul class="list-disc ml-5">
            <li>By default, the client revisits the page after each successful drag-save so the standard Rails flash notice can render.</li>
            <li>To opt into host-owned notifications, set <code>send_custom_event: true</code> on the drag-save form. This will dispatch a <code>recordingstudio:order:updated</code> event on <code>document</code> with a payload like <code>{ message, status, selected_order_recording_id, moving_recording_id, target_position }</code>.</li>
            <li>See the dummy app for a working example that logs the event payload to <code>console.log</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>